            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Bleach can remove surface mold from hard, non-porous surfaces, but EPA notes that biocides like bleach are generally not needed for routine cleanup; detergent and water work on hard surfaces, and porous materials may need to be discarded. Never mix bleach with ammonia or other cleaners. Fixing the moisture source matters more than which cleaner you use."
