          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Professional mold remediation typically costs roughly 1,500 to 6,000 dollars for a common job, less for a small contained area and well over 10,000 for attics, HVAC systems or whole-house damage. Containment, tear-out of porous materials, access and rebuilding decide where your bill lands.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If the moldy area is under about 10 square feet, EPA guidance says you can usually handle it yourself with the right protection and one of our <a href="/best-mold-remover/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-semibold hover:underline">best mold remover</a> picks. Whatever the size, fix the moisture first, or you will be paying for the same cleanup again.
          </p>
